hifiberry-songcompare (1.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Debian packaging. Builds the release binary and installs it as
    /usr/bin/songcompare; the package is named hifiberry-songcompare to match
    the rest of the HiFiBerry OS repository.
  * Build with the Rust 1.85 that Cargo.toml declares as the minimum. A let
    chain in the key-event loop is stable only from 1.88, so every toolchain
    between the two failed to compile the crate -- Debian trixie's 1.85.0
    among them, which is what this package is built with.
  * The unit tests run as part of the package build, so a broken build is
    caught where the .deb is made rather than only in CI.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 08:30:24 +0000
